-->\n<link rel=\"apple-touch-icon\" sizes=\"180x180\" href=\"/brand/apple-touch-icon.png\">\n<link rel=\"icon\" type=\"image/png\" sizes=\"32x32\" href=\"/brand/favicon-32.png\">\n<link rel=\"icon\" type=\"image/png\" sizes=\"192x192\" href=\"/brand/icon-192.png\">\n<link rel=\"manifest\" href=\"/brand/site.webmanifest\">\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\">\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"Open Practice\">\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"From idea to working page\">\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Open templates, sample data, code starters, and visual assets. Download, adapt, and build. One entry per resource, with handbook and practice-pack formats…\">\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://open-practice.open-practice.workers.dev/brand/og-1200x630.png\">\n<meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"1200\">\n<meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"630\">\n<meta property=\"og:image:alt\" content=\"Open Practice — practical AI learning, free and without signup\">\n<meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://open-practice.open-practice.workers.dev/builds/web.html\">\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\">\n<meta name=\"twitter:title\" content=\"The free AI practice library\">\n<meta name=\"twitter:description\" content=\"Handbooks, practice packs and offline HTML workspaces. No account needed to read.\">\n<meta name=\"twitter:image\" content=\"https://open-practice.open-practice.workers.dev/brand/og-1200x630.png\">\n<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#FDF7EE\">\n<meta name=\"twitter:twitter:title\" content=\"From idea to working page\"><meta name=\"twitter:twitter:description\" content=\"Open templates, sample data, code starters, and visual assets. Download, adapt, and build. One entry per resource, with handbook and practice-pack formats…\"></head><body><div class=\"site-bar\"><span>FREE PRACTICAL AI LEARNING · BUILD AT YOUR OWN PACE</span><span>OPEN MATERIALS · YOUR WORK TO KEEP</span></div><header class=\"hub-header\"><a class=\"brand\" href=\"/\" aria-label=\"Open Practice home\"><img src=\"/brand/open-practice-mark.svg\" width=\"42\" height=\"42\" alt=\"\"><span class=\"brand-type\">Open <em>Practice</em><small>PRACTICAL AI ENGINEERING</small></span></a><button class=\"nav-toggle\" id=\"nav-toggle\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"main-nav\">Menu</button><nav id=\"main-nav\" aria-label=\"Main navigation\"><div class=\"nav-group\"><a class=\"nav-top\" href=\"/academy/\" aria-current=\"page\">Academy</a><button class=\"nav-caret\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-label=\"Academy menu\">▾</button><div class=\"nav-menu\"><a href=\"/academy/\"><b>All courses</b><small>Project-based AI courses</small></a><a href=\"/curriculum.html\"><b>Curriculum map</b><small>How the paths connect</small></a><a href=\"/activities.html\"><b>50 activities</b><small>Short guided experiments</small></a><a href=\"/library.html\"><b>Free library</b><small>Handbooks and practice packs</small></a><a href=\"/dashboard.html\"><b>My learning</b><small>Your saved work</small></a></div></div><div class=\"nav-group\"><a class=\"nav-top\" href=\"/free-tools/\">Tools</a><button class=\"nav-caret\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-label=\"Tools menu\">▾</button><div class=\"nav-menu\"><a href=\"/free-tools/\"><b>39 free tools</b><small>Learn-by-doing workshops, no signup</small></a><a href=\"/tools.html\"><b>Tool field desk</b><small>Pick a task, get a practice prompt</small></a><a href=\"/ai-tools/\"><b>AI tools directory</b><small>What each tool is good for</small></a><a href=\"/llms/\"><b>LLM guide</b><small>Language models explained</small></a><a href=\"/compare/\"><b>Comparisons</b><small>Side-by-side, honest</small></a><a href=\"/tool-finder/\"><b>Tool finder quiz</b><small>Find a tool in 5 questions</small></a><a href=\"/prompts/\"><b>Prompt library</b><small>60 prompts to practise</small></a></div></div><div class=\"nav-group\"><a class=\"nav-top\" href=\"/learn/\">Learn</a><button class=\"nav-caret\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-label=\"Learn menu\">▾</button><div class=\"nav-menu\"><a href=\"/learn/beginners/\"><b>Start here</b><small>AI from zero</small></a><a href=\"/learn/seniors/\"><b>AI for seniors</b><small>Large print, safe steps</small></a><a href=\"/learn/kids/\"><b>AI for kids</b><small>Make things with a grown-up</small></a><a href=\"/glossary/\"><b>Glossary</b><small>AI words in plain language</small></a><a href=\"/tutorials/\"><b>Tutorials</b><small>Step-by-step builds</small></a><a href=\"/use-cases/\"><b>Use cases</b><small>AI for your kind of work</small></a></div></div><a class=\"nav-top\" href=\"/earn/\">Earn</a><a class=\"nav-top\" href=\"/api-keys/\">API Keys ✦</a><a class=\"nav-top\" href=\"/news.html\">News</a><a class=\"nav-top\" href=\"/community/\">Community</a><a class=\"nav-top nav-keys\" href=\"/settings/\" title=\"Your AI key settings\" aria-label=\"Key settings\">🔑<span class=\"nav-keys-label\"> Key settings</span></a><button id=\"account-open\">Sign in / Join ↗</button></nav></header><main><article class=\"reading-page\"><section class=\"info-hero\"><div><div class=\"eyebrow\">PROJECT 04 / Build with AI</div><h1>From idea to working page</h1><p>Build a simple calculator, understand its code, and test its edge cases.</p><p>Foundation · 5h estimated · 6 activities</p><div class=\"actions\"><a class=\"primary\" href=\"/?course=web\">Open editable workspace →</a><a href=\"/resources/packs/web-practice-pack.zip\" download>Complete practice pack ↓</a><a href=\"/resources/handbooks/web-handbook.md\" download>Handbook ↓</a></div></div><img src=\"/brand/covers/web.svg?v=illustrated-20261021\" width=\"410\" height=\"520\" alt=\"From idea to working page — illustrated handbook\"></section><section><h2>Before you begin</h2><ul><li>Can create/open a local HTML file.</li><li>A modern browser; coding experience is not required.</li></ul><p>Free original, non-accredited practice. Self-review is not independent assessment. No particular provider, payment platform or country is mandatory; use a legitimate available route or explicitly labelled manual practice.</p></section><section id=\"activity-1\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">ACTIVITY 1 / 35 MIN ESTIMATED</div><h2>Specify the smallest tool</h2><p class=\"lesson-explanation\">A useful first web tool has one clear job and no unnecessary accounts, payments, analytics, or personal data. Build a fictional quote calculator: quantity multiplied by unit price. Inputs must be finite, non-negative numbers. Decide whether decimals and zero are allowed before asking AI for code.\n\nAcceptance criteria turn an idea into something testable. Define inputs, expected results, error messages, keyboard behaviour, and offline use. This makes it possible to reject generated code that looks attractive but does the wrong thing. The calculator is an estimate exercise, not a production billing system.</p><h3>Worked example</h3><pre>ACCEPTANCE: 3 × 5 = 15.00; 0 × 5 = 0.00; 1.5 × 2 = 3.00; negative or blank input is rejected. Every input has a visible label. The page works without a network request.</pre><h3>Your practical task</h3><ol><li>Write a one-sentence problem statement.</li><li>Choose rules for zero, decimal, blank, negative, and non-finite values.</li><li>Create at least eight input/expected-result tests using quote-tests.json.</li><li>Sketch the page with labels, calculate action, result, and error area.</li><li>State explicitly that no payment or real customer data is involved.</li></ol><h3>Evidence to keep</h3><ul><li>A small written specification and page sketch.</li><li>Eight acceptance tests with expected values.</li><li>A clear boundary between an estimate and an invoice.</li></ul><h3>Mistakes to watch for</h3><ul><li>Starting from visual styling before defining behaviour.</li><li>Letting generated code decide how invalid inputs are handled.</li></ul><h3>Check your understanding</h3><p>If the tool displays 0.00 for a blank quantity, did it meet your specification?</p><h3>No-service / offline route</h3><p>Write the specification and test table on paper before coding.</p></section><section id=\"activity-2\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">ACTIVITY 2 / 50 MIN ESTIMATED</div><h2>Build and inspect</h2><p class=\"lesson-explanation\">Ask for one self-contained HTML file with labelled inputs, a button, a result area, and no external libraries. Read generated code before running it. Look for network calls, script imports, credential fields, unexpected storage, and operations unrelated to the tool’s purpose.\n\nSeparate calculation logic from the interface. A pure calculateQuote function can be tested with known inputs; the event handler reads form values and displays the result. Avoid inserting user-provided content with innerHTML. Use textContent for results and errors so input is treated as text rather than markup.</p><h3>Worked example</h3><pre>LOGIC: reject blank input; convert to numbers; reject non-finite or negative values; multiply; check that the result is finite; format for display.\nINTERFACE: read fields → call calculation → put a result/error into a text node.\nSCOPE: no tax, currency conversion, or payment processing.</pre><h3>Your practical task</h3><ol><li>Create or generate a one-file implementation matching your specification.</li><li>Inspect it for fetch, external script tags, storage, and unrelated permissions.</li><li>Find the function that validates and multiplies values.</li><li>Explain each validation branch in your own words.</li><li>Open it locally and run the happy-path tests before styling it.</li></ol><h3>Evidence to keep</h3><ul><li>An inspectable self-contained HTML file.</li><li>An explanation of input validation and calculation.</li><li>A list of external dependencies: none for this build.</li></ul><h3>Mistakes to watch for</h3><ul><li>Running generated install commands without inspection.</li><li>Assuming HTML min attributes replace all validation logic.</li></ul><h3>Check your understanding</h3><p>Which lines would you inspect first if a generated calculator unexpectedly requested an API key?</p><h3>No-service / offline route</h3><p>Use the supplied self-contained reference calculator and annotate the code before changing it.</p></section><section id=\"activity-3\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">ACTIVITY 3 / 45 MIN ESTIMATED</div><h2>Test and share</h2><p class=\"lesson-explanation\">Run the same acceptance tests against your actual file, not a screenshot or an AI explanation. Record expected output, observed output, and pass/fail. Test keyboard operation and a narrow screen as well as arithmetic. A page that works only with a mouse is not complete.\n\nThe reference calculator intentionally remains simple. JavaScript floating-point arithmetic can be unsuitable for precise financial accounting. Formatting with two decimals does not solve every money-calculation problem. State that limitation rather than advertising the exercise as an invoicing or payment system.</p><h3>Worked example</h3><pre>TEST LOG: quantity 3, price 5 → expected 15.00 → observed 15.00 → pass.\nKEYBOARD TEST: Tab reaches both inputs and Calculate; Enter submits; the result is announced in a status region.\nLIMITATION: Educational estimate, no tax or financial rounding policy.</pre><h3>Your practical task</h3><ol><li>Run all eight fixture cases and record observed results.</li><li>Navigate the page using only Tab, Shift+Tab, Enter, and Space.</li><li>Test a phone-width viewport and long error text.</li><li>Disconnect the network and repeat a successful calculation.</li><li>Share the HTML with a README listing tests and limitations.</li></ol><h3>Evidence to keep</h3><ul><li>Eight recorded arithmetic/validation tests.</li><li>Keyboard, narrow-screen, and offline checks.</li><li>A README that does not overstate financial correctness.</li></ul><h3>Mistakes to watch for</h3><ul><li>Testing the reference file while sharing a different untested version.</li><li>Treating two-decimal formatting as a complete accounting policy.</li></ul><h3>Check your understanding</h3><p>Can someone open the file offline and reproduce your test results without installing anything?</p><h3>No-service / offline route</h3><p>The entire activity is designed to run from a local file.</p></section><section id=\"activity-4\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">ACTIVITY 4 / 45 MIN ESTIMATED</div><h2>Debug with reproducible failures</h2><p class=\"lesson-explanation\">A useful bug report contains the smallest input that reproduces the problem, the expected result, the actual result, and the relevant environment. When asking AI for help, include the narrow function and test—not secrets, an entire account export, or unrelated application files.\n\nChange one thing at a time and keep a known-working version. A suggested fix may solve one case while breaking another. Rerun the full small test set after each change. If the model proposes a large rewrite, ask it to explain why a smaller patch is insufficient.</p><h3>Worked example</h3><pre>BUG: Empty quantity shows zero instead of an error.\nCAUSE: Number(&quot;&quot;) becomes 0.\nSMALL FIX: Check the trimmed raw input before numeric conversion.\nREGRESSION TESTS: zero must still be accepted; blank must fail.</pre><h3>Your practical task</h3><ol><li>Introduce the blank-input bug in a copy of the calculator.</li><li>Write a four-part bug report with exact reproduction steps.</li><li>Ask for or propose the smallest change that addresses the cause.</li><li>Run the blank and zero tests, then all remaining cases.</li><li>Record the diff and the reason the fix is correct.</li></ol><h3>Evidence to keep</h3><ul><li>A reproducible bug report.</li><li>A small explained patch and regression test results.</li><li>An unchanged known-working backup.</li></ul><h3>Mistakes to watch for</h3><ul><li>Pasting an entire private project into a cloud prompt.</li><li>Accepting a rewrite without checking whether old tests still pass.</li></ul><h3>Check your understanding</h3><p>Why must zero remain a separate test after fixing blank-input handling?</p><h3>No-service / offline route</h3><p>Debug the local file using browser developer tools or a text editor.</p></section><section id=\"activity-5\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">ACTIVITY 5 / 45 MIN ESTIMATED</div><h2>Improve accessibility and safe rendering</h2><p class=\"lesson-explanation\">Accessibility and safe rendering are engineering requirements, not final decorations. Use visible labels connected to inputs, meaningful button text, readable contrast, and a result/status region. Errors should explain the problem without relying only on red colour.\n\nTreat any future free-text field as untrusted. For this exercise, test that text such as &lt;img src=x onerror=alert(1)&gt; is shown as text or rejected, never executed. Do not add a rich-text editor or third-party UI library just to display a result. Keep the file inspectable and responsive.</p><h3>Worked example</h3><pre>REQUIRED: label for=&quot;quantity&quot; matches input id=&quot;quantity&quot;.\nSTATUS: a result region uses role=&quot;status&quot;.\nSAFE OUTPUT: result.textContent = message.\nREVIEW: controls remain readable at browser zoom and do not require hovering.</pre><h3>Your practical task</h3><ol><li>Check the label/input associations.</li><li>Confirm that errors are understandable without colour.</li><li>Inspect every location that displays user-supplied text.</li><li>Test keyboard focus visibility and a larger browser zoom.</li><li>Remove decorative features that reduce clarity or add unnecessary dependencies.</li></ol><h3>Evidence to keep</h3><ul><li>An accessibility checklist with observed results.</li><li>No untrusted HTML insertion in the tool.</li><li>A responsive version that remains usable without hover.</li></ul><h3>Mistakes to watch for</h3><ul><li>Using placeholders as the only labels.</li><li>Confusing a sanitisation claim with evidence that rendering is safe.</li></ul><h3>Check your understanding</h3><p>How would a keyboard user know which input is invalid and where the current focus is?</p><h3>No-service / offline route</h3><p>Perform every check on the downloaded HTML; no account or network is required.</p></section><section id=\"activity-6\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">ACTIVITY 6 / 80 MIN ESTIMATED</div><h2>Capstone: release a tested quote tool</h2><p class=\"lesson-explanation\">Deliver a small release that another person can inspect, run offline, and test. Include the implementation, specification, acceptance tests, observed results, accessibility notes, and known limitations. A release note should explain what changed and what is deliberately outside scope.\n\nIf you publish the file online, review it again for secrets and dependencies. Do not add payment buttons or real customer collection to this capstone. Those features introduce additional financial, security, legal, and privacy responsibilities that this practice build has not addressed.</p><h3>Worked example</h3><pre>RELEASE PACK: index.html, README.md, specification.md, test-results.md, CHANGELOG.md.\nACCEPTANCE: all eight fixture tests pass; keyboard and offline checks pass; no network dependencies; no misleading billing claims.</pre><h3>Your practical task</h3><ol><li>Freeze a release candidate and run the entire test checklist.</li><li>Ask another learner to reproduce two tests from the README.</li><li>Fix one issue they find and record the change.</li><li>Score the five capstone criteria with evidence.</li><li>Export the HTML and release pack without credentials or private data.</li></ol><h3>Evidence to keep</h3><ul><li>A runnable and inspectable release pack.</li><li>Complete tests and a documented review improvement.</li><li>Explicit limits covering financial accuracy, tax, and production use.</li></ul><h3>Mistakes to watch for</h3><ul><li>Publishing a later untested version after finishing the test report.</li><li>Claiming secure or production-ready solely because the page runs.</li></ul><h3>Check your understanding</h3><p>Which acceptance test would catch a regression introduced by your last visual change?</p><h3>No-service / offline route</h3><p>Complete and distribute the release as local files; public deployment is optional.</p></section><section><h2>Capstone self-review</h2><p>Score each criterion 0 (missing), 1 (partial), or 2 (demonstrated). A self-review pass needs at least 8/10 and 2/2 on the final safety/limits criterion. This is practice feedback, not verified assessment.</p><ul><li><strong>Specification</strong>: Inputs, invalid cases and scope are defined before implementation.</li><li><strong>Behaviour</strong>: All eight fixture tests have expected and observed results.</li><li><strong>Accessible use</strong>: Visible labels, keyboard operation, focus and status/error handling are checked.</li><li><strong>Reproducibility</strong>: Offline file, README, change log and review evidence are supplied.</li><li><strong>Safety and scope — critical</strong>: No secrets/dependencies/real payments; financial limits are stated.</li></ul><h2>Review questions</h2><details><summary>When should you execute generated code?</summary><p>After inspecting it and understanding its permissions</p><p>Check the relevant worked example and its evidence/authority boundary.</p></details><details><summary>Why test zero separately after rejecting blanks?</summary><p>Because fixing blank handling must not accidentally reject a valid zero.</p><p>Blank and zero have different meanings in the specification.</p></details><details><summary>Which method is appropriate for showing untrusted text in a result region?</summary><p>textContent</p><p>textContent treats the input as text instead of executable markup.</p></details><h2>Practice files</h2><ul><li><a href=\"/resources/curriculum/web/LICENCE.md\" download>LICENCE.md</a></li><li><a href=\"/resources/curriculum/web/quote-engine.mjs\" download>quote-engine.mjs</a></li><li><a href=\"/resources/curriculum/web/quote-lab.html\" download>quote-lab.html</a></li><li><a href=\"/resources/curriculum/web/quote-tests.json\" download>quote-tests.json</a></li><li><a href=\"/resources/curriculum/web/release-checklist.md\" download>release-checklist.md</a></li></ul><h2>References and editorial limits</h2><p>Original authored practice material; not independently expert-reviewed.</p><ul><li><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn_web_development/Getting_started/Your_first_website\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">MDN: first website</a></li><li><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn_web_development/Extensions/Forms/How_to_structure_a_web_form\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">MDN: accessible forms</a></li><li><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Node/textContent\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">MDN: textContent</a></li></ul><p><a href=\"/builds/index.html\">Browse all build paths →</a> · <a href=\"/curriculum.html\">Curriculum overview</a></p></section></article></main><footer><div class=\"hub-footer\"><div><a class=\"brand\" href=\"/\"><img src=\"/brand/open-practice-mark.svg\" width=\"44\" height=\"44\" alt=\"\">OPEN PRACTICE</a><p>Free, practical AI learning. Built to be used — not just watched.</p><p class=\"footer-small\">Independent · non-degree · non-accredited<br>A <a href=\"https://jacarandalabs.pages.dev/\">Jacaranda Labs</a> venture<br>Code: MIT · Original lessons: CC BY 4.0</p></div><div><h2>Learn</h2><a href=\"/academy/\">Academy courses</a><a href=\"/learn/beginners/\">Start here</a><a href=\"/learn/seniors/\">AI for seniors</a><a href=\"/learn/kids/\">AI for kids</a><a href=\"/glossary/\">Glossary</a><a href=\"/tutorials/\">Tutorials</a></div><div><h2>Build</h2><a href=\"/free-tools/\">39 free tools</a><a href=\"/earn/\">Earn by Doing</a><a href=\"/prompts/\">Prompt library</a><a href=\"/api-keys/\">Free API keys</a><a href=\"/settings/\">Key settings</a><a href=\"/tool-finder/\">Tool finder</a><a href=\"/library.html\">Free library</a></div><div><h2>Explore</h2><a href=\"/ai-tools/\">AI tools directory</a><a href=\"/llms/\">LLM guide</a><a href=\"/compare/\">Comparisons</a><a href=\"/use-cases/\">Use cases</a><a href=\"/news.html\">News</a><a href=\"/community/\">Community</a></div><div class=\"policy-links\" role=\"navigation\" aria-label=\"Policies and help\"><a href=\"/about.html\">About</a><a href=\"/help.html\">Help & FAQ</a><a href=\"/privacy.html\">Privacy policy</a><a href=\"/cookies.html\">Cookies & storage</a><a href=\"/terms.html\">Terms of use</a><a href=\"/licensing.html\">Licensing</a><a href=\"/accessibility.html\">Accessibility</a><a href=\"/contact.html\">Contact</a></div></div></footer><script type=\"module\" src=\"/learner.js\"></script><script type=\"module\" src=\"/growth.js\"></script><script type=\"module\" src=\"/nav.js\"></script></body></html>","binary":false,"etag":"\"f072b72e2801ae04\""},"/byok.js":{"body":"// Bring-your-own-key client. Requests go from this browser straight to the provider.\n// Keys are never sent to Open Practice. Default storage is this tab only (sessionStorage).\nconst STORE='op-byok-v1';\nexport const PROVIDERS={\n groq:{label:'Groq',guide:'/api-keys/groq/',hint:/^gsk_/,chat:'https://api.groq.com/openai/v1/chat/completions',models:'https://api.groq.com/openai/v1/models',prefer:['llama-3.3-70b-versatile','openai/gpt-oss-20b','openai/gpt-oss-120b','llama-3.1-8b-instant'],skip:/whisper|guard|tts|orpheus|playai|compound|prompt-guard|distil/i},\n gemini:{label:'Google Gemini (AI Studio)',guide:'/api-keys/google-gemini/',hint:/^AI/,models:'https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models?pageSize=200',prefer:['gemini-2.5-flash','gemini-flash-latest','gemini-2.5-flash-lite'],skip:/image|tts|live|embedding|aqa|vision|native-audio|robotics|computer|veo|imagen|pro/i},\n openrouter:{label:'OpenRouter (free models)',guide:'/api-keys/openrouter/',hint:/^sk-or-/,chat:'https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions',models:'https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models',prefer:['openrouter/free'],only:/:free$|^openrouter\\/free$/},\n mistral:{label:'Mistral (free Experiment plan)',guide:'/api-keys/mistral/',hint:/./,chat:'https://api.mistral.ai/v1/chat/completions',models:'https://api.mistral.ai/v1/models',prefer:['mistral-small-latest','open-mistral-nemo','ministral-8b-latest'],skip:/embed|moderation|ocr|voxtral|codestral-embed/i},\n cerebras:{label:'Cerebras',guide:'/api-keys/cerebras/',hint:/^csk-/,chat:'https://api.cerebras.ai/v1/chat/completions',models:'https://api.cerebras.ai/v1/models',prefer:['gpt-oss-120b','llama-3.3-70b','llama3.1-8b'],skip:/^$/}\n};\nfunction parse(text){try{const v=JSON.parse(text||'{}');return v&&typeof v==='object'&&!Array.isArray(v)?v:{}}catch{return {}}}\nfunction read(){let s={};try{s=parse(sessionStorage.getItem(STORE));if(!Object.keys(s).length)s=parse(localStorage.getItem(STORE))}catch{}return s}\nexport function loadSettings(){const s=read();const keys={},models={};for(const p of Object.keys(PROVIDERS)){if(typeof s.keys?.[p]==='string'&&s.keys[p])keys[p]=s.keys[p];if(typeof s.models?.[p]==='string'&&s.models[p])models[p]=s.models[p]}return {provider:PROVIDERS[s.provider]?s.provider:'',keys,models,remember:s.remember===true}}\nexport function saveSettings(s){const data=JSON.stringify({provider:s.provider,keys:s.keys,models:s.models,remember:!!s.remember});try{if(s.remember){localStorage.setItem(STORE,data);sessionStorage.removeItem(STORE)}else{sessionStorage.setItem(STORE,data);localStorage.removeItem(STORE)}}catch{throw new Error('This browser blocked storage. Your key cannot be kept; use the guided template instead.')}window.dispatchEvent(new Event('op-byok-change'))}\nexport function clearSettings(){try{localStorage.removeItem(STORE);sessionStorage.removeItem(STORE)}catch{}window.dispatchEvent(new Event('op-byok-change'))}\nexport function activeRoute(){const s=loadSettings();const p=s.provider&&s.keys[s.provider]?s.provider:Object.keys(s.keys)[0];return p?{provider:p,key:s.keys[p],model:s.models[p]||'',label:PROVIDERS[p].label}:null}\nfunction friendly(status,provider){\n const name=PROVIDERS[provider]?.label||provider;\n if(status===401||status===403)return `${name} rejected the key (HTTP ${status}). Check you copied the whole key, that it is not revoked, and that the service is available in your country. Guide: ${PROVIDERS[provider]?.guide||'/api-keys/'}`;\n if(status===429)return `${name} says you hit a rate or daily limit (HTTP 429). Wait a minute, try a smaller request, or switch provider in Key settings. Your work is saved.`;\n if(status===404)return `${name} could not find that model (HTTP 404). Open Key settings and press “Test key” to pick an available model.`;\n if(status===402)return `${name} needs credit for this model (HTTP 402). Choose a free model in Key settings.`;\n return `${name} returned an error (HTTP ${status}). Try again, or use the guided template.`;\n}\nasync function getJSON(url,headers,signal){const r=await fetch(url,{headers,signal,referrerPolicy:'no-referrer'});if(!r.ok)throw Object.assign(new Error('models'),{status:r.status});return r.json()}\nfunction headersFor(provider,key){if(provider==='gemini')return {'x-goog-api-key':key};const h={Authorization:'Bearer '+key};if(provider==='openrouter'){h['HTTP-Referer']=location.origin;h['X-Title']='Open Practice'}return h}\nexport async function listModels(provider,key,signal){\n const p=PROVIDERS[provider];if(!p)throw new Error('Unknown provider');\n let data;try{data=await getJSON(p.models,headersFor(provider,key),signal)}catch(e){if(e.status)throw new Error(friendly(e.status,provider));throw new Error('Could not reach '+p.label+'. Check your connection; some networks block AI services.')}\n let ids=provider==='gemini'?(data.models||[]).filter(m=>(m.supportedGenerationMethods||[]).includes('generateContent')).map(m=>String(m.name).replace(/^models\\//,'')):(data.data||[]).map(m=>String(m.id));\n if(p.only)ids=ids.filter(id=>p.only.test(id));if(p.skip)ids=ids.filter(id=>!p.skip.test(id));\n if(provider==='openrouter'&&!ids.includes('openrouter/free'))ids.unshift('openrouter/free');\n return [...new Set(ids)].sort((a,b)=>rank(p,a)-rank(p,b)||b.localeCompare(a,undefined,{numeric:true}));\n}\nfunction rank(p,id){const i=p.prefer.indexOf(id);return i>=0?i:/preview|exp|latest|lite/i.test(id)?120:99}\nasync function resolveModel(route,signal){if(route.model)return route.model;const ids=await listModels(route.provider,route.key,signal);if(!ids.length)throw new Error('No usable free text model was found for this key. Open Key settings.');const s=loadSettings();s.models[route.provider]=ids[0];try{saveSettings(s)}catch{}return ids[0]}\nexport async function chat(route,messages,{maxTokens=1100,temperature=0.7,signal}={}){\n if(!route?.key)throw new Error('No key saved. Add one in Key settings, or use the guided template.');\n const model=await resolveModel(route,signal),provider=route.provider;let r;\n try{\n  if(provider==='gemini'){\n   const system=messages.filter(m=>m.role==='system').map(m=>m.content).join('\\n\\n');\n   const contents=messages.filter(m=>m.role!=='system').map(m=>({role:m.role==='assistant'?'model':'user',parts:[{text:m.content}]}));\n   r=await fetch('https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models/'+encodeURIComponent(model)+':generateContent',{method:'POST',signal,referrerPolicy:'no-referrer',headers:{...headersFor(provider,route.key),'Content-Type':'application/json'},body:JSON.stringify({systemInstruction:system?{parts:[{text:system}]}:undefined,contents,generationConfig:{maxOutputTokens:maxTokens,temperature}})});\n  }else{\n   r=await fetch(PROVIDERS[provider].chat,{method:'POST',signal,referrerPolicy:'no-referrer',headers:{...headersFor(provider,route.key),'Content-Type':'application/json'},body:JSON.stringify({model,messages,max_tokens:maxTokens,temperature,stream:false})});\n  }\n }catch(e){if(e.name==='AbortError')throw new Error('Stopped.');throw new Error('Could not reach '+PROVIDERS[provider].label+'. Check your connection, or use the guided template.')}\n if(!r.ok)throw new Error(friendly(r.status,provider));\n const data=await r.json();\n const text=provider==='gemini'?(data.candidates?.[0]?.content?.parts||[]).map(x=>x.text||'').join(''):data.choices?.[0]?.message?.content;\n if(typeof text!=='string'||!text.trim())throw new Error('The model returned an empty answer. Try again or pick another model in Key settings.');\n return {text:text.replace(/<think>[\\s\\S]*?<\\/think>/g,'').trim(),model,provider};\n}\n","binary":false,"etag":"\"c41b2d776e9a47a8\""},"/checks.js":{"body":"// Deterministic rubric checks. Same rules run with or without AI, so the learner always gets real feedback.\nexport const words=t=>(t.trim().match(/[\\p{L}\\p{N}][\\p{L}\\p{N}'’.-]*/gu)||[]).length;\nconst lines=t=>t.split(/\\r?\\n/).map(s=>s.trim()).filter(Boolean);\nconst sentences=t=>t.replace(/\\n+/g,' ').split(/(?<=[.!?])\\s+/).map(s=>s.trim()).filter(s=>words(s)>0);\nconst keyPhrase=v=>String(v||'').trim().split(/\\s+/).slice(0,3).join(' ').replace(/[.,;:!?]+$/,'').toLowerCase();\nexport function runChecks(checks,text,values={}){\n const t=String(text||''),lower=t.toLowerCase(),out=[];\n for(const c of checks||[]){\n  let pass=true,label=c.label,fix=c.fix,detail='';\n  switch(c.t){\n   case 'words':{const n=words(t);pass=(c.min==null||n>=c.min)&&(c.max==null||n<=c.max);label??=c.max==null?`At least ${c.min} words`:`Length is ${c.min??0}–${c.max} words`;detail=n+' words';fix??=n<(c.min??0)?`Add detail until you reach at least ${c.min} words.`:`Cut to ${c.max} words or fewer. Remove repetition first.`;break}\n   case 'chars':{const n=t.trim().length;pass=(c.min==null||n>=c.min)&&(c.max==null||n<=c.max);label??=`Length is ${c.min??0}–${c.max} characters`;detail=n+' characters';fix??=n>c.max?`Shorten to ${c.max} characters.`:`Add detail; aim for at least ${c.min} characters.`;break}\n   case 'eachline':{const ls=lines(t).filter(l=>!c.skip||!new RegExp(c.skip,'i').test(l));const bad=ls.filter(l=>l.length>c.max);pass=ls.length>0&&!bad.length;label??=`Every line is ${c.max} characters or fewer`;detail=bad.length?bad.length+' line(s) too long':'';fix??=`Shorten each line to ${c.max} characters.`;break}\n   case 'lines':{const n=lines(t).filter(l=>!c.match||new RegExp(c.match,c.flags??'i').test(l)).length;pass=(c.min==null||n>=c.min)&&(c.max==null||n<=c.max);label??=c.max==null?`Has at least ${c.min??1} ${c.what||'lines'}`:`Has ${c.min??0}–${c.max} ${c.what||'lines'}`;detail=n+' found';fix??=c.max==null?`Add more ${c.what||'lines'} until you have at least ${c.min}.`:n>c.max?`Cut down to ${c.max} ${c.what||'lines'} or fewer.`:`Add more ${c.what||'lines'} until you have at least ${c.min??0}.`;break}\n   case 'has':{const v=keyPhrase(values[c.field]);pass=!v||lower.includes(v);label??=`Mentions your ${c.name||c.field}`;fix??=`Use “${String(values[c.field]||'').trim()}” in the text so the reader knows it is about them.`;break}\n   case 'any':{const hit=c.terms.some(x=>lower.includes(x.toLowerCase()));pass=hit;label??=c.label;fix??=c.fix;break}\n   case 'not':{const m=t.match(new RegExp(c.re,c.flags??'i'));pass=!m;label??='Avoids weak phrasing';detail=m?'Found: “'+m[0]+'”':'';fix??='Remove or rewrite: “'+(m?m[0]:'')+'”.';break}\n   case 're':{pass=new RegExp(c.re,c.flags??'i').test(t);break}\n   case 'count':{const n=(t.match(new RegExp(c.re,(c.flags??'i')+'g'))||[]).length;pass=(c.min==null||n>=c.min)&&(c.max==null||n<=c.max);detail=n+' found';break}\n   case 'blanks':{const m=t.match(/\\[\\[[^\\]]*\\]\\]/g)||[];pass=!m.length;label??='Every [[blank]] in the template is filled in';detail=m.length?m.length+' left':'';fix??='Replace each [[…]] with your own words. Start with: '+(m[0]||'');break}\n   case 'sentence':{const long=sentences(t).filter(s=>words(s)>c.max);pass=!long.length;label??=`No sentence is longer than ${c.max} words`;detail=long.length?long.length+' long sentence(s)':'';fix??='Split this sentence: “'+(long[0]||'').slice(0,90)+'…”';break}\n   case 'question':{pass=/\\?/.test(t);label??='Includes a question';fix??='Add one question the reader can answer.';break}\n   default:pass=true;\n  }\n  out.push({label:label||c.t,pass,fix:fix||'',detail});\n }\n return out;\n}\n// Shared quality checks for AI-flavoured filler that most writing tools want removed.\nexport const FILLER='\\\\b(in today\\'s (fast-paced|digital) world|unlock(ing)? the (power|potential)|delve|game[- ]changer|revolutioni[sz]e|as an ai( language model)?|elevate your|seamless(ly)?|leverage synergies|look no further)\\\\b';\n","binary":false,"etag":"\"4aa85f52242932a3\""},"/collection.js":{"body":"export function mountCollection(courses,{onOpen,onDownload}){\n const $=s=>document.querySelector(s),stage=$('#browse-stage');if(!stage||!courses.length)return;let index=0,start=null;\n function select(next){\n  index=(next+courses.length)%courses.length;const c=courses[index];\n  $('#browse-counter').textContent='BUILD PATH '+(index+1)+' OF '+courses.length;\n  $('#browse-cover').src='/brand/covers/'+c.id+'.svg?v=illustrated-20261021';$('#browse-cover').alt=c.title+' practice handbook';\n  $('#browse-track').textContent=c.track+' · Guided practice';$('#browse-title').textContent=c.title;$('#browse-project').textContent=c.project;$('#browse-description').textContent=c.description;$('#browse-time').textContent=c.time;\n  $('#browse-outcome').textContent=c.outcomes[0];$('#browse-safety').textContent=c.outcomes[c.outcomes.length-1];$('#browse-handbook').href=c.downloads.handbook;\n  $('#browse-primary').onclick=()=>onOpen(c);$('#browse-download').onclick=()=>onDownload(c);\n }\n const prev=$('#browse-prev'),next=$('#browse-next');prev.onclick=()=>select(index-1);next.onclick=()=>select(index+1);\n function navigate(e){\n  if(!['ArrowLeft','ArrowRight','Home','End'].includes(e.key)||e.altKey||e.ctrlKey||e.metaKey||e.shiftKey)return;\n  if(e.target!==stage&&e.target!==prev&&e.target!==next)return;\n  e.preventDefault();select(e.key==='Home'?0:e.key==='End'?courses.length-1:index+(e.key==='ArrowRight'?1:-1));\n }\n stage.onkeydown=navigate;\n const swipe=$('#browse-swipe');swipe.onpointerdown=e=>{if(e.target.closest('button,a')||e.isPrimary===false||(e.pointerType==='mouse'&&e.button!==0))return;start={x:e.clientX,y:e.clientY,id:e.pointerId};swipe.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId)};\n swipe.onpointerup=e=>{if(!start||e.pointerId!==start.id)return;const dx=e.clientX-start.x,dy=e.clientY-start.y;if(Math.abs(dx)>55&&Math.abs(dx)>Math.abs(dy)*1.2)select(index+(dx<0?1:-1));start=null};\n swipe.onpointercancel=swipe.onlostpointercapture=()=>{start=null};select(0)\n}\n","binary":false,"etag":"\"19e565720099f2a9\""},"/community/index.html":{"body":"<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\"><title>Open Practice community: learn and build together · Open Practice</title><meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\"><meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"Open Practice\"><meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Open Practice community: learn and build together\"><meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Join the free Open Practice communities on Whop, Discord, Telegram and Facebook: starter challenges, facilitator kits and ways to improve open AI lessons…\"><meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://open-practice.open-practice.workers.dev/community/\"><meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://open-practice.open-practice.workers.dev/brand/og-card.png\"><meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\"><link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/style.css\"><link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/hub.css\"><link rel=\"icon\" type=\"image/svg+xml\" href=\"/brand/open-practice-mark.svg\"><meta name=\"color-scheme\" content=\"light\"><meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#7c1f16\"><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://open-practice.open-practice.workers.dev/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Community\", \"item\": \"https://open-practice.open-practice.workers.dev/community/\"}]}</script><meta name=\"description\" content=\"Join the free Open Practice communities on Whop, Discord, Telegram and Facebook: starter challenges, facilitator kits and ways to improve open AI lessons…\"><link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://open-practice.open-practice.workers.dev/community/\"><meta name=\"twitter:twitter:title\" content=\"Open Practice community: learn and build together\"><meta name=\"twitter:twitter:description\" content=\"Join the free Open Practice communities on Whop, Discord, Telegram and Facebook: starter challenges, facilitator kits and ways to improve open AI lessons…\"></head><body><div class=\"site-bar\"><span>FREE PRACTICAL AI LEARNING · LEARN BY DOING</span><span>NO SIGNUP NEEDED · YOUR WORK STAYS YOURS</span></div><header class=\"hub-header\"><a class=\"brand\" href=\"/\" aria-label=\"Open Practice home\"><img src=\"/brand/open-practice-mark.svg\" width=\"42\" height=\"42\" alt=\"\"><span class=\"brand-type\">Open <em>Practice</em><small>PRACTICAL AI ENGINEERING</small></span></a><button class=\"nav-toggle\" id=\"nav-toggle\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"main-nav\">Menu</button><nav id=\"main-nav\" aria-label=\"Main navigation\"><div class=\"nav-group\"><a class=\"nav-top\" href=\"/academy/\">Academy</a><button class=\"nav-caret\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-label=\"Academy menu\">▾</button><div class=\"nav-menu\"><a href=\"/academy/\"><b>All courses</b><small>Project-based AI courses</small></a><a href=\"/curriculum.html\"><b>Curriculum map</b><small>How the paths connect</small></a><a href=\"/activities.html\"><b>50 activities</b><small>Short guided experiments</small></a><a href=\"/library.html\"><b>Free library</b><small>Handbooks and practice packs</small></a><a href=\"/dashboard.html\"><b>My learning</b><small>Your saved work</small></a></div></div><div class=\"nav-group\"><a class=\"nav-top\" href=\"/free-tools/\">Tools</a><button class=\"nav-caret\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-label=\"Tools menu\">▾</button><div class=\"nav-menu\"><a href=\"/free-tools/\"><b>39 free tools</b><small>Learn-by-doing workshops, no signup</small></a><a href=\"/tools.html\"><b>Tool field desk</b><small>Pick a task, get a practice prompt</small></a><a href=\"/ai-tools/\"><b>AI tools directory</b><small>What each tool is good for</small></a><a href=\"/llms/\"><b>LLM guide</b><small>Language models explained</small></a><a href=\"/compare/\"><b>Comparisons</b><small>Side-by-side, honest</small></a><a href=\"/tool-finder/\"><b>Tool finder quiz</b><small>Find a tool in 5 questions</small></a><a href=\"/prompts/\"><b>Prompt library</b><small>60 prompts to practise</small></a></div></div><div class=\"nav-group\"><a class=\"nav-top\" href=\"/learn/\">Learn</a><button class=\"nav-caret\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-label=\"Learn menu\">▾</button><div class=\"nav-menu\"><a href=\"/learn/beginners/\"><b>Start here</b><small>AI from zero</small></a><a href=\"/learn/seniors/\"><b>AI for seniors</b><small>Large print, safe steps</small></a><a href=\"/learn/kids/\"><b>AI for kids</b><small>Make things with a grown-up</small></a><a href=\"/glossary/\"><b>Glossary</b><small>AI words in plain language</small></a><a href=\"/tutorials/\"><b>Tutorials</b><small>Step-by-step builds</small></a><a href=\"/use-cases/\"><b>Use cases</b><small>AI for your kind of work</small></a></div></div><a class=\"nav-top\" href=\"/earn/\">Earn</a><a class=\"nav-top\" href=\"/api-keys/\">API Keys ✦</a><a class=\"nav-top\" href=\"/news.html\">News</a><a class=\"nav-top\" href=\"/community/\" aria-current=\"page\">Community</a><a class=\"nav-top nav-keys\" href=\"/settings/\" title=\"Your AI key settings\" aria-label=\"Key settings\">🔑<span class=\"nav-keys-label\"> Key settings</span></a><button id=\"account-open\">Sign in / Join ↗</button></nav></header><main class=\"hub-main wide\"><nav class=\"crumbs\" aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\"><a href=\"/\">Home</a> › <span aria-current=\"page\">Community</span></nav><div class=\"community-split\"><div class=\"community-main\"><section class=\"hub-hero\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">COMMUNITY</div><h1>Learn together, build in public</h1><p class=\"lede\">Open Practice is free and open. The community is how it gets better: share what you built, help someone stuck, run a session, or improve the lessons themselves.</p></section><div class=\"hub-grid hub-grid-2\"><a class=\"hub-card\" href=\"/starter.html\"><span class=\"hub-emoji\" aria-hidden=\"true\">🏁</span><small>DO IT</small><b>Starter challenge</b><span>A 120-minute challenge to run alone or with friends.</span></a><a class=\"hub-card\" href=\"/facilitators.html\"><span class=\"hub-emoji\" aria-hidden=\"true\">🧑‍🏫</span><small>TEACH</small><b>Facilitator kit</b><span>Run a free session for your class, club or team.</span></a><a class=\"hub-card\" href=\"https://github.com/king-kunta-cpu/open-practice\"><span class=\"hub-emoji\" aria-hidden=\"true\">🛠️</span><small>CONTRIBUTE</small><b>Improve the lessons</b><span>Report a mistake or suggest a lesson on GitHub.</span></a><a class=\"hub-card\" href=\"/free-tools/\"><span class=\"hub-emoji\" aria-hidden=\"true\">🚀</span><small>SHIP</small><b>Ship something this week</b><span>Pick one tool, finish it, share the link.</span></a></div><section class=\"hub-section\"><h2>Community guidelines</h2><ul class=\"hub-list\"><li>Share real work and honest results — including what did not work.</li><li>Never share API keys, passwords or other people’s private data.</li><li>Credit sources and tools you used.</li><li>Be kind to beginners; everyone started at lesson one.</li></ul></section></div><aside class=\"community-join\" aria-labelledby=\"join-h\"><h2 id=\"join-h\">Join a free community</h2><p>Pick the app you already use. Every community is free: share what you built, get u